Expanded story:
Amy stirred the sizzling eggs on her stove while Will tugged at his spoon and Amber giggled over toast crumbs. The kitchen hummed with ordinary morning chatter until an unsteady shuffling burst through the front door. A lone zombie, its eyes glazed white, staggered inside, a slow groan echoing off the walls.

Amy’s heart leapt; she scooped Will into her arms and pulled Amber behind her, both kids squealing as they ran toward the back stairwell. She shoved them into the small closet that served as their safe spot, slamming the door shut with a thud. The children hugged each other tight, breathing shallowly.

She stepped out onto the kitchen floor, wiping sweat from her brow. In the corner behind the fridge, she slipped open a hidden panel and pulled out a pistol, its matte black grip cool in her palm. She slid a gleaming katana into the slot beside it, the blade catching the light of the overhead bulb.

The first zombie lunged at her from the hallway; Amy fired the pistol, the bullet striking the undead’s chest and sending it collapsing to the floor with a wet thud. A second one staggered in through the back door—she swung the katana, slicing its neck cleanly as it fell. One after another, zombies surged forward: she shot, sliced, stabbed, each kill followed by the groan of new arrivals that kept coming.

When the last zombie finally collapsed at her feet, a single breath escaped from Amy’s lips; the kitchen was silent except for the thud of its body hitting the floorboards. She turned toward the closet door, where Will and Amber waited with wide eyes. The children stepped out into the hallway together as she followed them back to their safe spot.

The front door stood locked behind them, the night outside a quiet, moonlit backdrop. Amy held her kids close, both of them breathing in relief, and they all settled there—Will and Amber by her side—as the last zombie’s groan faded into silence.
